    {
      "name": "init_strategy",
      "docs": [
        "The MarketMaker `owner` creates and pays for its own Strategy; the MarketMaker must be live (not frozen or halted). Born frozen by the owner (reviews bytecode, then unfreezes via edit_strategy_status), and also `frozen_admin` unless the MarketMaker has permissionless_strategies set — in which case the admin must validate and unfreeze it. The protocol fee is stamped from GlobalConfig.default_protocol_fee_bps, not chosen by the owner (admin may override per-strategy via edit_strategy_fees). `base_id`/`quote_id` index into the MarketMaker's asset table; the strategy is bound to that pair for life. `base_mint`/`quote_mint` are validated against that table and exist so instruction parsers can read the pair off the creation ix without an account load. `quotes_account` is optional and may be bound later via update_strategy_quotes. `price_probe_base`/`price_probe_quote` are per-side input-atom sizes off-chain routers use to probe the price curve; the program stores them verbatim (both must be non-zero — a 0 is rejected) and they are updatable later via set_price_probe."
      ],
